# Copy this file to config/nosshpw_authorized_keys (which git ignores) and put
# the SSH PUBLIC key(s) for the key-only user (NOSSHPW_USER in config/build.env,
# default "nosshpw") here, one per line, e.g.:
#   cp ~/.ssh/nosshpw_ed25519.pub config/nosshpw_authorized_keys
# This user has no password, so these keys are its only way in. It runs sudo
# without a prompt. Use a different key than the one in config/authorized_keys
# (the build refuses the same key in both). Server ISO and Raspberry Pi only.
# Example:
# ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... automation@laptop
